---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy & Journalistic Integrity Standards"
  description="newskrypt editorial policy: strict rules on non-duplicate images, exact 55-character titles, zero keyword cannibalization, YMYL disclosures, and independence."
  canonicalUrl="https://crypto-news-rose.vercel.app/editorial-policy"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-20">
    <header class="mb-10 pb-6 border-b border-slate-200">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/30 rounded-full text-xs font-extrabold text-cyan-800 uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">
        <span>🛡️ Official Publication Standards</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black text-black tracking-tight mb-3">
        Editorial Standards, Publishing Rules & YMYL Guidelines
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-medium">Last Reviewed & Formally Ratified: September 2026 | Editorial Board & Integrity Desk</p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-sm text-black leading-relaxed">
      <!-- Section 1: Core Journalistic Integrity -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>1. Journalistic Integrity & Primary Source Verification</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-black mb-3">
          <strong>newskrypt</strong> operates under traditional canons of financial journalism: impartiality, absolute factuality, and rigorous multi-source verification. Every news report, market analysis, and regulatory breakdown published on our platform is verified through primary documentation - including official regulatory filings (SEC, BaFin, MiCA, CFTC), court dockets, audited smart contract bytecode, and cryptographic on-chain proofs before publication.
        </p>
        <p class="text-black">
          Our editorial team maintains zero tolerance for unverified rumors, speculative market manipulation, or uncredited aggregation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Strict Publishing & Editorial Rules -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>2. Mandatory Publishing & SEO Editorial Standards</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-black mb-4">
          To maintain superior reading experiences, search engine compliance, and zero content overlap, <strong>newskrypt</strong> enforces four mandatory publishing standards across all news stories and features:
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-black text-base mb-1">Rule A: Non-Duplicate Visual Assets & Image Compliance</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-800 text-xs sm:text-sm">
              Every published article must feature between <strong>1 and 3 distinct, contextual images</strong> (1 hero image + up to 2 supporting charts/infographics). <strong>newskrypt strictly prohibits image reuse</strong>: no image URL or file is ever repeated across multiple articles. Every hero image includes custom descriptive <code class="bg-white px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-black font-mono border border-slate-300">imageAlt</code> and <code class="bg-white px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-black font-mono border border-slate-300">imageCaption</code> metadata matching the article's exact subject matter.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-black text-base mb-1">Rule B: Unique Headings & Title Length Constraints</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-800 text-xs sm:text-sm">
              Every article title and H1 heading is <strong>100% unique</strong> across the publication. Article metaTitles must not exceed 58 characters (calibrated to <strong>exact 55-character targets</strong>) to prevent SERP truncation and align precisely with primary keywords. Section headings (H2, H3) within an article must be distinct, descriptive, and non-repetitive.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-black text-base mb-1">Rule C: Fresh Keyword Targeting & Non-Cannibalization</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-800 text-xs sm:text-sm">
              Each new article targets a fresh primary topic and angle without keyword cannibalization or topic duplication with previously published stories. Article tags must accurately reflect specific protocols, entities, or regulatory frameworks covered in that story.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-black text-base mb-1">Rule D: Strict Meta Description Standards</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-800 text-xs sm:text-sm">
              Every story carries a concise, highly informative metaDescription calibrated to <strong>exact 155-character standards</strong>, providing readers and search engines with complete context before click-through.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: YMYL & Financial Disclaimers -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3">3. YMYL & Financial Advisory Disclaimers</h2>
        <p class="text-black mb-3">
          As a digital financial news publication operating under Google’s <strong>Your Money Your Life (YMYL)</strong> quality standards, <strong>newskrypt</strong> adheres to strict financial disclosure guidelines:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-black">
          <li><strong>No Personalized Financial Advice:</strong> All analytical reports, price charts, order flow metrics, and yield assessments published on <strong>newskrypt</strong> are strictly for informational, educational, and news reporting purposes. No content constitutes personalized investment, tax, legal, or financial advice.</li>
          <li><strong>Independent Due Diligence:</strong> Readers are strongly urged to perform independent research and consult licensed financial advisors before making any capital allocations or trading decisions.</li>
          <li><strong>Risk Acknowledgment:</strong> Digital assets and crypto derivatives carry high market volatility and capital risk. <strong>newskrypt</strong> bears no liability for trading decisions or capital losses incurred by market participants.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Commercial Independence & Sponsored Content Firewall -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3">4. Commercial Independence & Advertising Firewall</h2>
        <p class="text-black mb-3">
          An impermeable firewall separates the <strong>newskrypt</strong> newsroom from commercial, advertising, and corporate sponsorship teams:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-black">
          <li>Advertisers, sponsors, and token issuers exert zero influence over story selection, editorial tone, or investigative findings.</li>
          <li>Any paid promotion or press release is conspicuously tagged with a prominent <strong>"Sponsored Content"</strong> or <strong>"Press Release"</strong> banner.</li>
          <li>Outbound links within paid material utilize mandatory <code class="bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-black font-semibold border border-slate-200">rel="sponsored nofollow"</code> attributes to uphold web index integrity.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Staff Personal Investment Ethics -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3">5. Staff Personal Investment & Trading Ethics</h2>
        <p class="text-black mb-3">To eliminate front-running and financial conflicts of interest:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-black">
          <li>Staff journalists and editors are prohibited from trading micro-cap tokens or altcoins about which they are actively reporting.</li>
          <li>Full-time editorial personnel must complete annual asset disclosure filings with our compliance officer.</li>
          <li>Journalists holding major benchmark assets (e.g., BTC, ETH) for long-term reserves must disclose relevant holdings in article author bylines.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6: Generative AI & Human Verification Standards -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3">6. Generative AI & Human Sign-off Standards</h2>
        <p class="text-black">
          Human critical thinking, investigative interviewing, and firsthand verification are essential to credible financial journalism. While automated tools assist with translation, formatting, or raw statistical sorting, <strong>every article published on newskrypt is researched, written, fact-checked, and signed off by a credentialed human journalist</strong>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>